{
  "category": "Tiny Mouse Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It is not yet skilled at storing electricity. It may send out a jolt if amused or startled.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite its small size, it can zap even adult humans. However, if it does so, it also surprises itself.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is unskilled at storing electric power. Any kind of shock causes it to discharge energy spontaneously.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "PICHU charges itself with electricity more easily on days with thunderclouds or when the air is very dry. You can hear the crackling of static electricity coming off this POKéMON.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "When PICHU plays with others, it may short out electricity with another PICHU, creating a shower of sparks. In that event, this POKéMON will begin crying, startled by the flash of sparks.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is still inept at retaining electricity. When it is startled, it discharges power accidentally. It gets better at holding power as it grows older.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite its small size, it can zap even adult humans. However, if it does so, it also surprises itself.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is not yet skilled at storing electricity. It may send out a jolt if amused or startled.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "The electric pouches on its cheeks are still small. They cannot store much electricity yet.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It plays with others by touching tails and setting off sparks. This appears to be a test of courage.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "The electric sacs in its cheeks are small. If even a little electricity leaks, it becomes shocked.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
